course: dictionary
lesson: 5701
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word loin is one of them, and the sentence around it tells you which meaning is wanted. «She cooked a pork loin for Sunday lunch.» The words pork and lunch are the clues: loin is a cut of meat.
explain: The older meaning is about the body. The loins are the part of the body around the hips and the lower belly. «Gird up your loins» is an old phrase that meant get ready for hard work or a fight.
explain: Always check the clues around the word, then try your meaning in the sentence. Be careful: loin is also a French word meaning far, but in English it does not mean far.
fact: Some English words have more than one meaning.
fact: «Loin» means a cut of meat from the back of an animal, between the ribs and the hips, as in «pork loin» and «loin chops».
fact: «Loins» in old use means the part of the body around the hips and lower belly.
fact: «Gird up your loins» means get ready for hard work or a fight.
fact: A «loincloth» is a cloth worn around the loins.
exercise: «She cooked a pork loin for dinner.» What is a loin in this sentence? | *A cut of meat from the back of an animal | A kind of cooking pot | A small sheep | A type of bread
exercise: «Gird up your loins» is an old phrase. What does it mean? | To sleep for a long time | *To get ready for hard work or a fight | To sing very loudly | To tie your shoelaces
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Gird up your loins» that means the part of the body around the hips. | up | your | *loins | gird
test: «The butcher sold us lamb loin chops.» What does loin mean here? | A part of a bicycle | A long walk | *A cut of meat | A type of hat
test: Which word is a cloth worn around the loins? | pork loin | *loincloth | sirloin | loin chop
exam: «Dad said, "Gird up your loins, we have a long hike ahead."» What does gird up your loins mean here? | Buy new walking boots | Go to sleep early | *Get ready for hard work | Eat a big dinner
